WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.780
"Hard work is sacred."

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.660
Just as I was recalling words like
these with a sigh of relief...

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.910
I heard a "toka-ton-ton"...

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.990
The sound seemed to ring faintly from afar.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.670
Suddenly, everything I'd done up
to that point struck me as foolish.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.250
I stood up, walked back to my room,

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.800
climbed under the covers, and went to sleep.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.800
Okay, that's far enough.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.430
Now, for the next passage...

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.720
Doumyouji.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.850
The next passage. Read it, please.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.940
I turned my face up

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.940
to face the sky high above.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.650
Cirrocumulus.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.950
Who told you to compose a haiku?!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.670
Tapirs live in equatorial jungles.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.920
Did you all know

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.800
that tapirs have an unusual
bone structure that makes

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.130
their front legs longer than their back legs?

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.300
But setting that aside...

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.430
I'm currently...

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.390
fleeing the Demon King's pursuit!

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.030
You gave me quite the run-around.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.410
You have a birthmark on your butt marking
you as the wielder of tremendous power.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.290
Show it to me!

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:02.910
No!

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.960
There are various reasons I can't show it to you!

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.840
You leave me no choice.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.710
In that case...

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.920
I'll tear it off by force!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.470
That's enough!
I'll tear it off by force!

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.260
What?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.260
Who are you?!

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:22.520
I am heir to the mark passed
down since ancient times.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.890
The one who will stand against the Demon King...

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.480
The one true hero: Tapir!

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.730
Demon King Veribadd, I won't
let you have your own way!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.240
Such impudence from a mere tapir!

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.530
Very well! Then, I shall start by ripping off y—

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.070
Super Tap-oom!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:43.790
That's huge! What <i>is</i> that spell?!
Super Tap-oom!

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.540
Super Tap-oom!

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.130
Amazing! That was amazing, Tapir!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.020
Have you learned the power of pay-to-win items?

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.690
I get it now, Tapir...

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:14.690
So...

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.400
So that's what "tap-oom" meant...

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.490
Hey! Touno! Wake up!

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.490
Hey, kids! Don't fall sleep in class, ya hear?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.120
I really, really can't stand bugs!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.050
A while ago, there was a centipede
four centimeters long in my house.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.010
And I just shouted...

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.260
Monnu!

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.760
...out of nowhere.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.800
That's a hard word to say
on the spur of the moment.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.140
But, Natsuki, four centimeters is really big!

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:48.140
It's about as large as an eleven-week-old fetus!

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.020
Why are you comparing it to new life?!

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.940
I see.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.280
By the way, speaking of sizes...

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.150
A toilet flush has settings for
both "big" and "small,"

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.410
but even if you set it for "small,"
it still uses a lot of water.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.990
That doesn't really have much to do with size.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.580
And what kind of subject is
that for a heroine to bring up?

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.160
No...

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.580
I don't care! Continue!

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.670
For some reason, Botan
just gave the "Go" sign!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.420
I just think,

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.510
if you used the "small" setting
for "big," "middle," <i>and</i> "small,"

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.260
it would save water and be
good for the environment.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.350
I feel I should ask... What's "middle"?

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.560
When it's almost a liquid, it's "middle"!

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.190
Okay, <i>stop</i>!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.900
Please wait a moment.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.580
Hm?

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:57.250
Oh, dear.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.210
My mechanical pencil's out of lead.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.050
I'll go buy some for you.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.220
What? But...

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.590
I was about to go to the school store anyway...

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.180
I'll buy you some while I'm there.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.470
Really?

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.470
Well, if you wouldn't mind...

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.600
This should cover it, right?

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.020
You want me to buy the whole box?

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.530
Well, there are 40 leads in a case,
and they're 200 yen apiece,

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.440
which comes to 8,000 yen, right?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.990
The 200 yen is obviously for all 40 leads!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.320
What kind of bourgeois writing
materials were you expecting?!

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:30.540
I-It's 200 yen for the whole case?

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.210
You mean to say that each lead is only five yen?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.460
What is this quantum physical pricing?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.170
Is that the antonym of "astronomical"?

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.590
First time I've ever heard that!

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.560
Hello?

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:53.560
Natsunoji.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.230
"Natsunoji"?

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.060
There's something I'd like to show you.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.940
Could I trouble you to pay a visit to the roof?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.070
What's this character supposed to be?

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:03.320
Just—

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:04.200
You'll see when you get there.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.080
So what is it?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.080
What'd you call me up here to show me?

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:20.840
I'm Ai!

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.090
I'm Karin!

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:26.260
Together, we are... Aikarin!

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.850
It's time for "Aikarin's Machine Gun Short Skits!"

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.900
Delinquent.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.820
Hey, I wanna hit the arcade.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.030
Lend me some cash, would ya?

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:48.990
Oh, no! I can't!

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:53.330
Oh, yeah? You sure that's your final answer?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.210
My li'l bro's the leader of
an elementary school gang!

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:57.750
That's pathetic!

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.000
28 points.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.510
That's harsh!

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:08.180
I deducted five points in advance because
you made up another nickname for me.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.970
Which means I was already in the
red when I called you up here?

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.560
Even with those five points,
you'd still be in the red.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:17.140
Plus, you called it "machine gun,"
but you only did one gag.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.190
That makes no sense.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:22.480
Well, we thought this one gag was as
powerful as a machine gun barrage...

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.440
That makes no sense! It has to be rapid fire!

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:27.190
So why did you suddenly
decide to take on comedy?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:31.200
Well... earlier, I saw a
comedy program on TV, and...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.080
I thought "That looks easy.
Even I could reach the top level."

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.000
Do you have an eternal wellspring of
confidence inside that brain of yours?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.380
Huh?

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.750
Far away?

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:53.390
It's time for "Aikarin's Explosive
Hand Grenade Short Skits!"

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.510
Birth!

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:56.890
What's wrong?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.270
Huh? Are you okay?

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.480
I-I'm giving birth!

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:04.150
I know! The Lamaze Technique!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.580
Oxygen is delicious!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:19.040
Why did you take the surrealist route?

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:19.910
What do you think?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.170
I'm not sure what to say.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.920
That reminds me, Furuishi...

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:25.960
It's Furuhashi!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.630
So your first name's Ai, is it?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.920
I never knew!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:35.890
We spent three years in middle
school together, didn't we?!

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:37.470
And with that...

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.100
...Chronicles of the Going Home Club...

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.350
...has completed all twelve episodes.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.440
Thank you for watchi—

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.940
It's not over yet!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.840
What?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.300
I get another appearance?!

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.350
But I thought last week was the final episode...

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:19.100
President! Urgent news!

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:21.680
Is it about the Soccer Club
and the Baseball Club?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.100
You already know about it?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.060
Don't worry. I've already taken
measures to deal with it.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.860
What do you mean?

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.860
I've sent the vice president to the scene.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.240
Iizuka?!

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:39.200
The animators got complacent and forgot
to design the secretary, Kaneda-kun.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.380
The Student Council Vice President, Iizuka Kouhei.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:51.880
They call him a romantic... an idealist.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.300
So he has an alias, too...

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.470
His ability is "The Perfect Equal."

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.510
Another one with superpowers?!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:04.230
What kind of ability is "The Perfect Equal"?

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:08.270
From what I've heard, it ensures lunch
portions are served out equally.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.190
What's the point of that?!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:13.110
Plus, our school doesn't even have lunch service.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.200
In other words, his ability is useless garbage, right?

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.490
I think that's a little too harsh.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.870
Speaking of aliases...

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.830
We call dogs "bow-wows" so why
don't we call cats "meow-meows"?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.500
That's less an alias and more of a label.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.340
That's true.

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.970
It's the same with Malay Tapirs.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:36.880
Ta...

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:41.430
Why did you bring up an animal when
you don't know what sound it makes?!

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.560
We could call Parrots
"Pollywannacracker-chan," too.

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.230
Good morning!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.560
Now we're just talking about
things that don't matter!

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:51.610
And a whip-poor-will should be
called "Whip-poor-will-chan"!

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.610
That's the same thing!

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.860
You people are real idiots!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:01.450
We still haven't reached that cute
sundries shop we saw on the internet?

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.910
According to the map, it should be in this area...

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.750
Knowing Sakura,

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.120
she probably brought a
map of the world by mistake.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.500
That's not the punchline here, is it?

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:17.630
The scale's way too big!

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.720
You are currently... here!

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.260
I can barely even tell
where our solar system is!

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:27.020
Well, shall we stop by the convenience
store, and then head to the park?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.570
You can do it!

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.780
Claire! Look at this!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:45.160
This is the most delicious part of the ice cream!

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.460
May I try it?

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.420
Yes!

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.170
So this is the taste of the commoners?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.630
That overjoyed reaction just shows

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.800
how big the gap is between you and the commoners.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.640
I did have one of those before.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.100
There were these guys
who wanted to get rid of me

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.810
before I could learn Hagitsuki-ryuu.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.820
That sounds awfully savage.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.070
I was about three years old.

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.860
They used a sniper rifle to shoot me in the chest.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.780
That's a major incident out of the blue!

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:30.410
I was such a novice.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.580
I didn't even notice the sniper one kilometer away.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.920
Of course, now, I'd spot him immediately.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.130
You sound embarrassed about your past,

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.590
but it's scarier that you notice them at all!

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:43.430
B-But you were shot in the chest...

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:47.600
Does that mean you died when
you were a child, Botan?!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.600
Karin, calm down.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:53.980
The fact that she's here with us now
proves that she survived being shot.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:56.770
But, how did you survive?

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.990
I happened to be carrying
something in my chest region.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:03.740
It blocked the bullet.

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:06.080
Wow! Just like in the movies!

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.040
Yes. I got it from my parents.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.870
My ribcage!

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.870
You can't block a bullet like that!

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.880
I've been waiting for this moment.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.670
It's time to settle this once and for all.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.680
Bear!

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.430
Um...

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.600
He is the strongest of the Four Bear Kings.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.190
Do you really think you can beat me?

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:46.490
It can't be...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.370
You mean...

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.080
It was you...

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.120
Karin?!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.250
What's going on here?

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:57.420
I am of a race that can
alter its contents at will.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.500
The Costume Bear!

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.090
And you're wide open...

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:02.590
Botan!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:12.810
Femi...

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:14.730
...nine...

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:16.310
ap...

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:18.110
...peal!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.230
Her feminine appeal is overwhelming...

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.280
I can't beat her.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:24.820
Naturally!

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.740
The Four Bear Kings are a
force to be reckoned with!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:27.870
But...

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.370
This doesn't even make any sense!

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:43.050
Look, everyone. This is
the famous Moldau River.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.260
It's so big!

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:46.970
Speaking of which, Sakura...

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:50.640
You sang "Die Moldau" in your
middle school choir, right?

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.560
That's right!

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.270
Well, since we're here now,
why don't you sing it?

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.440
I'd like to hear it!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.440
Please sing it in German!

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.020
In... In German?

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.610
Yes! Please!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.460
That's "Demon King," Sakura!

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.370
I want to hear "Die Moldau"!

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:25.300
Not "Demon King!" "Die Moldau," please!

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.470
You never sang "Die Moldau," did you?

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:39.770
Father!

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.060
That's not your father!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.520
By the way,

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.530
"Die Moldau" is actually
one part of a longer work

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:48.320
by a Czech composer named Smetana,
arranged for choruses to sing.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.950
The lyrics we sing were added by the Japanese.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:54.830
So when you sang it in middle
school, it was in Japanese?!

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:55.700
I'm sorry!

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.330
Karin. Here's your drink.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:04.000
I didn't want you to hurt your
hands, so I opened it first.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:08.590
I've also turned in your handouts for
the day, so don't worry about that.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:11.010
Then, I filled your mechanical pencil with lead,

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:14.600
and I put an extra pink eraser
in your locker for you.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.720
Do you have a handkerchief and pocket tissues?

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.720
Also, I went to the restroom for you.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:20.140
I know this is your usual routine, but...

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:23.940
don't you think you're spoiling
her a little too much?

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.480
Oh, no, I don't fink fo!

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:30.070
Goo!

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:34.240
That would never happen!

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.540
I thought up a "How to
Draw Natsuki song!

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.370
Huh?

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:43.130
The crescent moon rises high in the sky!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.630
That's it?!

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.340
For winning the title of MVP,

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:55.100
Cristiano Messi will be awarded
a top-of-the-line sports car.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:55.890
Wow!

00:17:55.890 --> 00:18:00.020
Soccer players drive big cars, huh?

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.570
I thought up a "How to Draw Sakura" song!

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.820
Then, I'll draw it now!

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.570
But there's something you need first.

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:12.200
A mental image.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.280
A mental image of what you're drawing is essential.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:14.360
This looks like it's gonna take a while. Better fast-forward.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.120
Understand? When it's time to draw—

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:25.540
And just like that, you've got Sakura!

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.540
Don't fast-forward through the drawing process!

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.050
Yeah, right! Yeah, right! Yeah, right!

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:31.420
Somewhere, hidden from the eyes of men,

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:36.680
there is a merciless underworld
organization that trains skilled Retorters.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.430
Yeah, right! Yeah, right! Yeah, right!

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.060
It is called:

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:40.140
Yeah, right! Yeah, right! Yeah, right!

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:41.640
The Retorters' Pit

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.310
That doesn't exist!

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:49.820
I now have two important announcements!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:53.450
The first concerns the cat that's been
hanging around the school grounds.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:56.410
That cat just had kittens
behind the school building.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:00.580
I thought she was looking chubby recently!

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:02.450
So she became a mom!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:04.790
Okay! Let's go see!

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.960
I'm sure they're all as cute as Karin.

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:10.550
I want to go see them!

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:12.460
Okay! Let's go see them now!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.800
W-Wait a minute! Before we do that...

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:19.220
What's the other important announcement?

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:23.230
Oh.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:26.520
It's that there are only 60 seconds
until the end of the series.

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:31.980
You decided to bring this up now?

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.780
Just fifty-four seconds remaining...

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.490
We only have time for one more joke.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.990
We can't bomb the final punchline.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:42.240
I want to see the kittens!

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.960
What? It's mine? What awful timing!

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.830
Natsuki, did you change your ringtone?!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.000
That's not the part you
should be concerned with!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.550
Furuhashi, sorry!

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:53.260
I'm a little occupied right now!

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:58.430
Natsukinov... You got my name
right for the first time.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:00.390
Huh? Wait, anyway...

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.260
What do you want?

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:05.890
I realized I keep forgetting to tell you.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.940
And given the occasion,
I thought I should tell you now...

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:14.110
You remember how I wasn't sure if I should join

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:16.610
the Tennis Club or the Hundred Poems Club?

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.160
The truth is...

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.120
I joined the Volleyball Club.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.790
Who cares about that?!

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:26.910
We're out of time!

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:02.800
Oh, well. I wish we could
have made it to Record 100.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:06.510
That would've been impossible in the time we had.

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:10.020
We could've done a skit every 45 frames.

00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:11.600
That'd make it possible, right?

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:15.190
My retorts couldn't keep up with that speed.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:16.980
We didn't get to do a final joke.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:21.110
We would have done better just showing
cute pictures of Karin the whole time.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:24.200
You never change, do you?

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.660
Karin?

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:33.160
The first evening star!

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:49.560
What?

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:50.890
It's moving, isn't it?

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:52.100
Um...

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:53.600
That's an airplane.

00:22:55.480 --> 00:22:57.940
Well, that ruined everything...
